      en: "Khirbet et-Tannur is a Nabataean temple on a hilltop in modern-day Jordan, about 70 km north of Petra. Built in the 2nd century BCE, it was dedicated to the goddess Atargatis. The temple is notable for its rich sculptural decoration, including reliefs of deities and animals. It served as a pilgrimage site and place of sacrifice. Its mountaintop location provided wide views and symbolized proximity to the gods. The temple was abandoned in the 4th century CE.",
