      en: "The Anjara Shrine, also known as Our Lady of the Mountain, is a Christian pilgrimage site in northwestern Jordan. Tradition holds that Jesus, Mary, and Joseph rested here during the Flight into Egypt. The modern church was consecrated in 2010 atop the remains of a 5th-century Byzantine church. The complex includes a monastery and a garden. Excavations uncovered Byzantine mosaics, which are preserved. Anjara attracts thousands of pilgrims annually, especially on August 15 for the Assumption. The site is also revered by Muslims for its connection to Mary.",
